---
const examples = [
  { city: 'New York', product: 'Flavour 03', image: 'newyork' },
  { city: 'Phoenix', product: 'Flavour 01', image: 'phoenix' },
  { city: 'Seattle', product: 'Flavour 02', image: 'seattle' },
];
---

<div class="retail-overview">
  <section
    class="ako-brief"
    id="forecasting-for-ako"
    aria-labelledby="ako-business-question"
  >
    <div>
      <div class="ako-label">
        <span class="ako-name">AKO</span>
        <span>
          Startup
          <br />
          Data-science case study
        </span>
      </div>
      <h2 id="ako-business-question">
        What should each store
        <br />
        <em>stock next?</em>
      </h2>
      <p>
        A case study completed for <strong>AKO</strong>, a startup working on
        retail demand forecasting and inventory decisions. The task: predict
        monthly sales for every product–store pair, to support purchasing,
        allocation and replenishment.
      </p>
      <p class="source-note">
        FashionDrink, the retailer in the brief, is fictional.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="brief-data">
      <p class="eyebrow">The forecasting brief</p>
      <dl class="scope-grid">
        <div>
          <dd>5</dd>
          <dt>products</dt>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dd>10</dd>
          <dt>US stores</dt>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dd>48</dd>
          <dt>months of history</dt>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dd>300</dd>
          <dt>exported forecasts</dt>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <div class="date-range">
        <span>
          <b>2013–2016</b>Observed sales
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <span>
          <b>Jan–Jun 2017</b>Requested forecasts
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="retail-eda" aria-labelledby="retail-demand-signals">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Explore before predicting</p>
        <h2 id="retail-demand-signals">
          Different products.
          <br />
          Different demand signals.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        I checked missing values and outliers, encoded{' '}
        <strong>10 event indicators</strong>, and compared sales across products
        and stores. Unusual prices and high sales were investigated before
        deciding to retain them.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="eda-grid">
      <figure>
        <h3>Compare the sales trajectories</h3>
        <img
          src="/media/retail-forecasting/demand-history.svg"
          width="640"
          height="365"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="Observed monthly sales from 2013 to 2016, summed across ten stores, with a separate line for each of the five products."
        />
        <figcaption>
          Monthly totals reveal different sales levels, seasonal patterns and
          changes over time.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <h3>Check associations product by product</h3>
        <img
          src="/media/retail-forecasting/correlations.svg"
          width="640"
          height="365"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="Pearson correlations with sales. Temperature: 0.53, 0.67, 0.47, 0.09 and 0.21 for Flavours 01 to 05. Price: −0.17, 0.18, 0.10, −0.50 and −0.28."
        />
        <figcaption>
          Pearson correlations over 48 months: total sales versus mean
          temperature or price across stores. Association does not establish
          causation.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="takeaway">
      <strong>A useful modeling clue:</strong> temperature correlates with
      Flavour 02 sales at <b>+0.67</b>, versus <b>+0.09</b> for Flavour 04.
      Product identity matters when combining these predictors.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="retail-model" aria-labelledby="retail-forecasting-model">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / From transactions to a model</p>
        <h2 id="retail-forecasting-model">
          Learn across stores.
          <br />
          Keep the sales history.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        One <strong>CatBoost regressor</strong> learns across all 50
        product–store series. It combines categorical identifiers with numerical
        context; lagged features provide the recent history for each series.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="preparation-strip">
      <span>
        <b>11,986</b> transaction records
      </span>
      <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
      <span>
        <b>2,400</b> monthly rows
      </span>
      <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
      <span>
        <b>1,950</b> rows with lags and targets
      </span>
    </div>
    <figure class="architecture">
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 700px)"
          srcset="/media/retail-forecasting/architecture-mobile.svg"
        />
        <img
          src="/media/retail-forecasting/architecture.svg"
          width="1180"
          height="360"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="32 monthly inputs, including 12 lag features, enter one shared CatBoost ensemble. Tree outputs combine into a sales forecast six months ahead. During training, actual target sales guide successive trees to correct remaining prediction errors. The drawn trees are schematic."
        />
      </picture>
      <figcaption>
        500 trees · depth 6 · learning rate 0.1 · RMSE training objective. Three
        categorical inputs: store, product and source month.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="model-notes">
      <div>
        <h3>Aggregate at the decision level</h3>
        <p>
          Sum sales by product, store and month; average prices and temperature;
          mark an event present if it occurs during the month.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Align history with the target</h3>
        <p>
          Use 1-, 2- and 3-month lags of sales, discounts and two market
          indicators. Each input row targets sales{' '}
          <strong>six months later</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="horizon-example"
      aria-label="The export maps July 2016 inputs to January 2017 sales, through December 2016 inputs to June 2017 sales."
    >
      <span class="eyebrow">How the export is built</span>
      <span>
        Jul 2016 inputs <b aria-hidden="true">→</b> Jan 2017 sales
      </span>
      <span>
        Dec 2016 inputs <b aria-hidden="true">→</b> Jun 2017 sales
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="retail-results" aria-labelledby="retail-forecasting-results">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Evaluate & deliver</p>
        <h2 id="retail-forecasting-results">
          Measure the error.
          <br />
          Make the forecast readable.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The notebook reports three complementary metrics, then exports a
        product–store–month forecast table. The figures below redraw the saved
        predictions alongside the observed sales history.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="evaluation">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Saved evaluation · random 70/30 split · 585 test rows
      </p>
      <dl class="metric-grid">
        <div>
          <dt>WAPE</dt>
          <dd>
            13.25<span>%</span>
          </dd>
          <p>Total absolute error divided by total actual sales.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>RMSE</dt>
          <dd>1,013.10</dd>
          <p>Error in sales-volume units, with more weight on large misses.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>R²</dt>
          <dd>0.93</dd>
          <p>Fit relative to a constant prediction of the test-set mean.</p>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="evaluation-note">
        <strong>Interpretation:</strong> the random split mixes time periods. A
        chronological backtest is still needed to estimate future-period
        accuracy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="forecast-grid">
      {examples.map((example) => (
        <figure>
          <h3>
            {example.city}
            <span>{example.product}</span>
          </h3>
          <img
            src={`/media/retail-forecasting/${example.image}-forecast.svg`}
            width="420"
            height="290"
            loading="lazy"
            alt={`${example.city}, ${example.product}: observed monthly sales in 2016 and saved forecasts for January to June 2017. Forecasts are dashed; 2017 actual sales are unavailable.`}
          />
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">
      The three examples used in the notebook, from the largest stores by 2016
      sales. Dashed lines are saved forecasts; 2017 actuals were not supplied.
      All three charts share the same sales-volume scale.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .retail-overview {
    margin-block: 2.5rem;
    --retail-blue: #446a79;
    --retail-rose: #aa6a56;
    --retail-paper: #f5f1e9;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.1vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.13;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 1.2rem;
    scroll-margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font: 600 0.95rem/1.5 var(--font-body);
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }
  p {
    color: #67685f;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  strong,
  b {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  figure {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--retail-rose);
  }
  .ako-brief {
    scroll-margin-top: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.12fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
    background: #eae0d7;
    border-top: 1px solid #b58f7e;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .ako-label {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
  }
  .ako-name {
    font: 700 3.6rem/0.9 var(--font-body);
    letter-spacing: -0.07em;
    color: #4c6268;
  }
  .ako-label > span:last-child {
    font: 0.63rem/1.8 var(--font-label);
    color: #796859;
    border-left: 1px solid #c5b6a6;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .ako-brief em {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--retail-rose);
  }
  .brief-data {
    background: #f5f1e9bd;
    padding: 1.7rem;
  }
  .brief-data > p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .scope-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.7rem 1rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 1.7rem;
  }
  .scope-grid dd {
    margin: 0;
    font: 2.9rem/1.1 var(--font-display);
    color: var(--retail-blue);
  }
  .scope-grid dt {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
  }
  .date-range {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #cec5b8;
  }
  .date-range span {
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .date-range b {
    display: block;
    font: 0.68rem/1.8 var(--font-label);
    color: var(--retail-rose);
  }
  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.3rem;
  }
  .section-heading p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .section-heading h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .retail-eda,
  .retail-model,
  .retail-results {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .eda-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.2rem;
  }
  .eda-grid figure,
  .forecast-grid figure {
    background: var(--retail-paper);
    padding: 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid #d7cfc3;
  }
  figcaption,
  .source-note {
    color: #777469;
    font-size: 0.67rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .takeaway {
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--retail-blue);
    background: #e6e8e2;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .preparation-strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .preparation-strip span {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .preparation-strip b {
    display: block;
    font: 1.7rem/1.3 var(--font-display);
    color: var(--retail-blue);
  }
  .preparation-strip i {
    font-style: normal;
    color: #8e958d;
  }
  .architecture {
    padding: 0.7rem 0.7rem 1rem;
    background: var(--retail-paper);
    border: 1px solid #d7cfc3;
  }
  .architecture figcaption {
    margin: 0.5rem 0.9rem 0;
  }
  .model-notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .model-notes p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.77rem;
  }
  .horizon-example {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    background: #e8e4dc;
  }
  .horizon-example > span {
    font-size: 0.69rem;
  }
  .horizon-example > .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.55rem;
  }
  .horizon-example b {
    color: var(--retail-rose);
    padding-inline: 0.35rem;
  }
  .evaluation {
    background: #e5e8e2;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem 1rem;
    border-top: 2px solid #7f9394;
  }
  .evaluation > .eyebrow {
    margin-top: 0;
    color: var(--retail-blue);
  }
  .metric-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 1.3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .metric-grid dt {
    font: 0.7rem/1.6 var(--font-label);
    color: var(--retail-blue);
  }
  .metric-grid dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0.7rem;
    font: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem)/1.2 var(--font-display);
  }
  .metric-grid dd span {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }
  .metric-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }
  .evaluation-note {
    border-top: 1px solid #c4ccc0;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.73rem;
  }
  .forecast-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .forecast-grid figure {
    padding: 0.9rem 0.65rem 0.4rem;
  }
  .forecast-grid h3 {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding-inline: 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .forecast-grid h3 span {
    font: 0.6rem/1.8 var(--font-label);
    color: var(--retail-rose);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .ako-brief,
    .section-heading {
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .horizon-example {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .horizon-example > .eyebrow {
      width: 100%;
    }
    .forecast-grid {
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .metric-grid {
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .ako-brief,
    .section-heading,
    .eda-grid,
    .model-notes,
    .forecast-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .ako-brief {
      scroll-margin-top: 2rem;
      gap: 1.4rem;
    }
    .brief-data {
      padding: 1.2rem;
    }
    .section-heading {
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .retail-eda,
    .retail-model,
    .retail-results {
      margin-top: 2.3rem;
      padding-top: 1.8rem;
    }
    .preparation-strip {
      padding: 0.9rem 0.3rem;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .preparation-strip span {
      font-size: 0.58rem;
    }
    .preparation-strip b {
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }
    .model-notes {
      gap: 1.2rem;
    }
    .horizon-example {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.7rem;
    }
    .evaluation {
      padding: 1.2rem;
    }
    .metric-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .metric-grid > div {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr;
      align-items: baseline;
      column-gap: 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #c4ccc0;
      padding-bottom: 0.8rem;
    }
    .metric-grid dd {
      grid-column: 1;
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
    .metric-grid p {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1 / 3;
    }
    .evaluation-note {
      border-top: 0;
      padding-top: 0;
    }
    .forecast-grid {
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
